Subject: EVO-X2 Scratch Build Absent Workspace Working Directory Contradiction

@ [fault_uuid] 9d93a084-b978-409d-850e-86d370e9b8ba
@ [canonical_uuid] 935e020f-8c6f-49e4-b355-63eabd3b778b
@ [local_core_bookend_commit] 1edd3a5596660b9789d7bf43eba82d2ee4917744

& [Observed]
  + the published semantic core required operation2 materialize_absent_workspace to report the final workspace root as its process working directory
  + ESBE-012 and ESBE-014 require that final workspace root to be absent until operation2 atomically establishes it
  + Windows process creation cannot use an absent directory as current directory, so the two requirements cannot both execute under the published mapping

& [Cause]
  + the predecessor plan's future working-directory coordinate was copied into the operation record without distinguishing execution base from materialization destination

& [Correction]
  + operation1 verify_source_archive executes from exact service root C:/AI/services/cantor-scratch-build-4fdd29cb
  + operation2 materialize_absent_workspace executes from existing parent C:/AI/workspaces and atomically establishes exact absent child C:/AI/workspaces/cantor-build-4fdd29cb through a unique sibling stage
  + operations3 through6 execute from the established workspace and operation7 from the target root
  + command arguments operations grants denials target roots and one-run authority remain unchanged

& [Status]
  + corrected locally during package/executor implementation and pending focused adversarial full-workspace publication gates
